= Docs: Phase 5 coverage campaign -- findings from 83.0% to 94.7%
Typed assigns, native lexical references and batches 2-5 take CORE.c encodability from 83.0%
to 94.2%; the mechanical tail and batch 11 reach 94.7% (the survey is an upper bound). What the
CORE.c compile taught: PE code size, a 145 s parse, the deopt cycle behind the abandoned
compiler roots; lazy refold and inlining across dispatch land. Regex was never a wall (it
encodes). Hash encodes: the bug was a general flat-named-arg defect. p6return's blocker: the
logical handler chain and the Java stack diverge at an engine frame; the unwind cannot reach it.
- 1ee9ab2df3 Docs: the typed assigns land at 83.0%; lexicalref is now the lever
- 444a7c2758 Docs: what the CORE.c compile taught -- PE code size, and 145s
