= Docs: Phase 5 coverage campaign -- conclusions and the final table
Day two takes CORE.c to 96.5%: batches 12-21 (with/without, the pure-op tail, uint params and
attributes, p6return as the SUCCEED handler's value, syscalls as the newdisp op mechanism with
the stat family, the backend directives removed). Unsigned boxing: box_u/unbox_u/set_uint and
the *param_u readers are unsigned and the line is drawn there; the wider chain (the compiler's
RT_UINT box, the binder sites, the container FETCH) is a separate task. Ops come from the
classlib registry, not by hand: it lands flat, redundant with the hand rows, which are deletable.
- 82d936703b Docs: Phase 5 day two -- batches 12-21, p6return, syscalls, directives, the uint box finding
- 18915391af Docs: batch 23 lands; the bytecode RT_UINT box is the last uint cause
- 04c39b8bbc Docs: ops come from the classlib registry, not by hand
- 1540d38b2a Docs: five signed sites for one native type (batch 24/24b)
- e12064e0b1 Docs: uint boxing beyond batch 23 reverted; the line is drawn there
- ab7e229ad4 Docs: the classlib registry lands flat -- redundant with the hand rows, hand cases now deletable
